{
  "raw": {
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Career-Advisor--Office-of-Career-Services_R4630-1": {
      "title": "Career Advisor, Office of Career Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Office of Career Services Career Advisor   Under the supervision of the Associate Director of Career Readiness and Education, the Career Advisor (Professional Services Specialist 3) delivers the strategic execution of the career planning and internship processes for students at all Kean University campuses including Union, Kean Ocean, Kean Jersey City and Kean Skylands and provides guidance and assistance to Wenzhou-Kean University, in China.  With a focus on career outcomes and career readiness support, the Career Advisor is responsible for ensuring effective career readiness advisement, student internship enrollment, internship course management and delivery of various internal programs that support students. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: overseeing a caseload of students for career counseling and advising; conducting internship course delivery; counseling students regarding internship and full time job opportunities; career preparation and planning; presenting to students on NACE competency development; providing vision and direction through effective academic and employer collaboration; contribute to hiring initiatives as led by the Office of Career Services; and performing related work as required. Kean’s Career Services Career Advisor empowers students' short- and long-term career preparation and management activities so they can meet their career and educational goals. This position requires travel and a flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours. Candidates must have the ability to travel to other campus locations and off campus locations for employer collaborations, internship engagement opportunities, field site visits and related activities. Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s degree and two years of professional experience in student support services, career services, human resources, a business environment or a related field is required. A Master’s degree in a related field may be substituted for one year of the required experience. Three years of professional experience working with students in an institution of higher education coordinating career services and internships is preferred. Candidates must have the ability to develop and foster strong professional relationships with students, alumni and employers, faculty and administrators; marketing experience and/or the ability to develop and implement effective strategies for promoting and increasing involvement in programs and services; excellent oral and written communication skills; and excellent customer service skills. Candidacy review begins immediately and continues until appointment is made.  Please submit your cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment. In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the negotiated annual salary range for this position is: $69,373.45 - $75,985.55 (Steps 2-4). Salaries for internal applicants will be based on union negotiated calculations. This position may also be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, including health and dental insurance, a retirement plan and benefits for work life balance. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Kean University Benefits website . Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Computer-Science-and-Technology_R2836": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Computer Science and Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nPart time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. The Dorothy and George Hennings College of Science, Mathematics and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Technology Adjunct Faculty Kean University  in Union, New Jersey has grown into a comprehensive, global institution of higher education serving a diverse enrollment of nearly 19,0000 students worldwide. Kean creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research and impactful public engagement. Kean, a proud R2 Research University, continues its legacy as a top producer of teachers in New Jersey and is a growing educational hub in the fields of business, health care and technology. Its six colleges – the College of Business and Public Management; the College of Education; the College of Liberal Arts; the Dorothy and George Hennings College of Science, Mathematics and Technology; Michael Graves College; and the College of Health Professions and Human Services - offer more than 50 undergraduate degrees over a full range of academic subjects. Kean also offers six doctoral degree programs and more than 70 options for graduate study leading to master’s degrees, professional diplomas or certifications. The University is also a higher education innovator within the State of New Jersey, partnering with Ocean County College, in Toms River, New Jersey and Brookdale Community College, in Lincroft, New Jersey, to provide access for students to earn a bachelor’s degree from Kean. The Kean Skylands campus, located in Jefferson Township, New Jersey, is designed to serve as an outdoor living laboratory for field-based scientific study and other classroom and field instruction. We are excited to invite Adjunct applications for upcoming semesters. Please note that Adjunct faculty positions at Kean University are filled on an as-needed basis. Qualified candidates may be contacted if, and when, there is an available opening or possible future opening. Computer Science –  to teach undergraduate level courses in-person at the Union or Jersey City campus. Courses may include Information Technology Foundations, Fundamentals of Artificial Intelligence, Computer Systems, Analysis of Algorithms, Computer Architecture, Web Programming, Java, Python and other related topics. Prior teaching experience preferred and daytime and evening courses are available. All adjunct positions are non-tenure track. They require a master’s degree in a related field and teaching experience unless otherwise indicated; candidates with an ABD, Ed.D., Ph.D. or other acceptable disciplinary doctorate are encouraged to apply. Proficiency in a Learning Management System is required, consistent with University guidelines. Adjunct faculty teaching one three (3) or four (4) credit class shall provide at least one (1) hour of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. An additional thirty (30) minutes of availability shall be provided for each additional class taught during the semester/session. Availability may be in person or virtual and shall be scheduled by the adjunct faculty member, taking into account student needs. Adjunct faculty teaching fewer than three (3) credits shall provide at least thirty (30) minutes of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. Regardless of the number of credits an Adjunct faculty member is teaching, they may, at their discretion, provide additional office hours beyond the amounts required. Kean University Adjuncts are paid in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement: Effective September 2025, the rate of pay is: $2,100 per credit. Effective September 2026, the rate of pay is: $2,225 per credit. Beginning in their 13th semester taught, Adjuncts receive an additional $75 per credit. Adjuncts are enrolled in a state administered retirement plan, when eligible, and may be eligible to enroll in the Part-Time State Health Benefits Program for medical and prescription drug coverage. Please visit this link for more information: Health Coverage for Adjuncts . Please submit a cover letter (indicating availability for days, evenings or weekends and preferred campus location), resume and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and be on-going. Official transcripts are required before appointment. Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Music_R4636": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Music",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. College of Liberal Arts, Department of Music Adjunct Faculty Kean University  in Union, New Jersey has grown into a comprehensive, global institution of higher education serving a diverse enrollment of nearly 19,0000 students worldwide. Kean creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research and impactful public engagement. Kean, a proud R2 Research University, continues its legacy as a top producer of teachers in New Jersey and is a growing educational hub in the fields of business, health care and technology. Its six colleges – the College of Business and Public Management; the College of Education; the College of Liberal Arts; the Dorothy and George Hennings College of Science, Mathematics and Technology; Michael Graves College; and the College of Health Professions and Human Services - offer more than 50 undergraduate degrees over a full range of academic subjects. Kean also offers six doctoral degree programs and more than 70 options for graduate study leading to master’s degrees, professional diplomas or certifications. The University is also a higher education innovator within the State of New Jersey, partnering with Ocean County College, in Toms River, New Jersey and Brookdale Community College, in Lincroft, New Jersey, to provide access for students to earn a bachelor’s degree from Kean. The Kean Skylands campus, located in Jefferson Township, New Jersey, is designed to serve as an outdoor living laboratory for field-based scientific study and other classroom and field instruction. We are excited to invite Adjunct applications for upcoming semesters. Please note that Adjunct faculty positions at Kean University are filled on an as-needed basis. Qualified candidates may be contacted if, and when, there is an available opening or possible future opening. Cello Studio –  to teach private cello lessons in-person and possibly assist with Chamber Music and Orchestra at the Union campus. Lesson scheduling to be arranged with students; Orchestra meets on Tuesday nights at 7:00 p.m. Expertise in cello pedagogy and experience in high-school level recruitment and outreach required. Applicants with an active performance career and community engagement are preferred. Violin Studio – to teach private violin lessons in-person and possibly assist with Chamber Music and Orchestra at the Union campus. Lesson scheduling to be arranged with students; Orchestra meets on Tuesday nights at 7:00 p.m. Expertise in violin pedagogy and experience in high-school level recruitment and outreach required. Applicants with an active performance career and community engagement are preferred. Music Specialist –  to teach classes, lessons, or ensembles in one or more of the following areas at the Jersey City campus: music theory, sight singing & ear training, music history, private studio lessons, music in general education (music survey, music fundamentals), and small ensembles. Applicants with prior experience in higher education and an active performance or related professional music career are preferred.  Opera Workshop – to lead the Opera Workshop program weekly on Saturday mornings, from 9am-11:45am at the Kean Union campus. All adjunct positions are non-tenure track. They require a master’s degree in a related field and teaching experience unless otherwise indicated; candidates with an ABD, Ed.D., Ph.D. or other acceptable disciplinary doctorate are encouraged to apply. Proficiency in a Learning Management System is required, consistent with University guidelines. Adjunct faculty teaching one three (3) or four (4) credit class shall provide at least one (1) hour of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. An additional thirty (30) minutes of availability shall be provided for each additional class taught during the semester/session. Availability may be in person or virtual and shall be scheduled by the adjunct faculty member, taking into account student needs. Adjunct faculty teaching fewer than three (3) credits shall provide at least thirty (30) minutes of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. Regardless of the number of credits an Adjunct faculty member is teaching, they may, at their discretion, provide additional office hours beyond the amounts required. Kean University Adjuncts are paid in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement: Effective September 2025, the rate of pay is: $2,100 per credit. Effective September 2026, the rate of pay is: $2,225 per credit. Beginning in their 13th semester taught, Adjuncts receive an additional $75 per credit. Please submit a cover letter (indicating availability for days, evenings or weekends and preferred campus location), resume and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin immediately and be on-going. Official transcripts are required before appointment. Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Associate-Director-of-Interior-Design--Office-of-Campus-Planning_R4652": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Interior Design, Office of Campus Planning",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Office of Campus Planning Associate Director of Interior Design   Under the supervision of the Director of Design and Space Management, the Associate Director of Interior Design (Associate Director 3) provides managerial oversight and direction for the day-to-day operations of renovation and refurbishment projects; coordinates and oversees the allocation and implementation of space projects; and establishes and implements interior design criteria for the Union, Jersey City, and satellite campuses of Kean University. The Associate Director oversees and coordinates the planning and development of interior design and space planning projects across all campus locations and affiliated work sites, providing project leadership from initial planning and development through implementation and completion.   The Associate Director performs project management responsibilities for assigned projects, establishes project priorities, coordinates internal and external resources, monitors project performance, and addresses issues affecting successful completion; ensures project timelines and budgets are developed, monitored and achieved; and oversees existing-condition evaluations, installation and renovation activities, vendor and contractor performance, and compliance with established design, operational, and project requirements; and performs related work as required.   This position requires travel, including travel to other campus locations and a flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours.   Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s degree; two years of professional experience supervising design, planning, furniture specification and relocation and space allocation; and a driver’s license valid in the State of New Jersey is required. This position also requires the ability to perform tasks that require moderate physical activity, including driving, walking long distances, standing, bending and/or stooping, lifting and carrying objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Candidate must have excellent oral and written communication skills; proficiency with AutoCAD; familiarity with Revit; experience with Microsoft 365 and associated software; and the ability to create space plans, furniture plans and finish schedules.   Candidacy review begins immediately and continues until appointment is made.  Please submit your cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment.   In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the annual salary range for this position is: $95,000 to $110,000. This position may also be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, including health and dental insurance, a retirement plan and benefits for work life balance. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Kean University Benefits website . Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Learning-Design-Technologist--Kean-Global_R4606-1": {
      "title": "Learning Design Technologist, Kean Global",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Kean Global Learning Design Technologist   The Learning Design Technologist (Professional Services Specialist 2) is a professional position at Kean Global reporting to the Director for Learning Design and Academic Technologies. The position is responsible for providing platform leadership and support and contributing to our learning experience design processes and projects. This position will intersect with and support the daily management and functioning of Kean Global’s creation and delivery of online courses and programs and provides faculty and student support. In addition to educational technologist functions like platform research, testing, and support, this position will perform a learning technology design function alongside instructional designers and departmental leadership. The position exists within a highly collaborative team environment. The Learning Design Technologist will be expected to work within an established team culture and user experience philosophy while providing thought leadership to help shape the future of Kean’s online learning experience. This position requires travel and a flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours. Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s degree and three years of professional experience working with learning management systems in an online learning setting within an institution of higher education or in education is required. A Master’s degree in a related field may be substituted for one year of the required experience. Experience with one or more of the following platforms is preferred: learning management systems, online proctoring, course materials management systems, publisher courseware. Experience with one or more of the following web technologies is also preferred: HTML, CSS, JavaScript. Candidate must have strong technical knowledge and the ability to navigate technical support and multiple priorities; strong interpersonal skills and the ability to accomplish simultaneous tasks; and excellent oral and written communication skills.   Candidacy review begins immediately and continues until appointment is made.  Please submit your cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment. In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the negotiated annual salary range for this position is: $84,131.83 - $103,245.42 (Steps 3-8). Salaries for internal applicants will be based on union negotiated calculations. This position may also be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, including health and dental insurance, a retirement plan and benefits for work life balance. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Kean University Benefits website . Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Facilities-Operations-and-Events-Manager--Office-of-Facilities-and-Operations_R4632": {
      "title": "Facilities Operations and Events Manager, Office of Facilities and Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Office of Facilities and Operations Facilities Operations and Events Manager Under the supervision of the Director of Facilities, the Facilities Operations and Events Manager (Managing Assistant Director 2) is responsible for supporting and managing facilities operations across the University, including events management, vendor coordination, service coordination, building inspections, turnover support, moving services and other operational activities.  The Manager will be directly responsible for overseeing facilities operations as assigned by the Director and/or Assistant Vice President.   The Manager supports the Facilities leadership team with managing day-to-day activities; collaborates with the operations team and liaises with the facilities team to ensure conducive process and project coordination; participates in the multitude of planning stages that take place leading up to events and transportation dates; and manages the communication of all necessary updates to the appropriate colleagues and team members.    In addition to events, the Manager serves as an operational resource for the Office of Facilities and Operations by coordinating assigned facilities services and supporting University-wide operational needs. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: managing elevator service calls, managing pest control scheduling and service needs, coordinating moves and furniture relocation requests, conducting building cleanliness inspections, assisting with Residence Life, Faculty Housing and Guest Housing turnover inspections and meeting with vendors regarding facilities work and service requests.   This position requires travel and a flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours. This is an essential employee position. This employee is required to oversee facilities operations as the on-call manager on duty, which requires on-campus presence during weather and/or emergency situations.   Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s degree; two years of professional work experience in facilities management, operations management, event management/planning, project management, higher education or related field; and a driver’s license valid in the State of New Jersey is required. Related experience in higher education is highly preferred. Applicants who do not possess the required education may substitute the required experience on a year-for-year basis. NOTE: This position also requires the ability to perform essential functions that require moderate physical activity including, but not limited to: driving, walking long distances/standing for long durations of time outdoors/indoors, bending and/or stooping, lifting and carrying objects weighing up to 50 pounds. Candidate must have proficiency in Office 365 and basic computer operations; excellent oral and written communication skills; a strong focus on customer service; and the ability to work a flexible schedule and be the on-call on-site manager.   Candidacy review begins immediately and continues until appointment is made.   Please submit your cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment.   In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the annual salary range for this position is: $78,000 to $90,000. This position may also be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, including health and dental insurance, a retirement plan and benefits for work life balance. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Kean University Benefits website . Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Managing-Assistant-Director-of-Strategic-Initiatives--Office-of-Strategic-and-Global-Initiatives_R4633": {
      "title": "Managing Assistant Director of Strategic Initiatives, Office of Strategic and Global Initiatives",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Office of Strategic and Global Initiatives Managing Assistant Director of Strategic Initiatives   Under the direction of the Vice President of Strategic and Global Initiatives, the Managing Assistant Director of Strategic Initiatives (Managing Assistant Director 2) manages the development and support of programming in Strategic and Global Initiatives. Established in 2015, the Strategic and Global Initiatives division plays a pivotal role in coordinating innovative projects, cultivating strategic partnerships, and spearheading special initiatives for the university. The division encompasses several essential departments including: Strategic Initiatives, the Office of Career Services, the Center for International Studies, Kean Skylands, the Human Rights Institute, the Holocaust Resource Center and Council on Global Education and Citizenship.   The Managing Assistant Director develops, manages and leads initiatives as assigned that promote and support the mission and values of the University. At the direction of the Vice President, this employee oversees certain administrative and operational affairs, conducts research, develops papers and proposals and supports the development of the new programming housed in the division. The Managing Assistant Director oversees partnerships, such as those with College Steps, New Jersey Clean Communities, the PA of NYNJ and other organizations and also manages the operations of the annual Full Steam Ahead pre-college program, Work-Earn-Live-Learn (WELL) program and other division pre-college programs. Other work may include the development of new employer and external partnerships.   The Managing Assistant Director also supports the Chancellor’s office operations as assigned related to the Wenzhou-Kean University location in Wenzhou, China, as well as planning, logistics and operations related to international delegation visits and travel both to and from Kean University. This position requires travel and a flexible schedule including evening and weekend hours. International travel may be required, including travel to China.   Qualifications: Graduation from an accredited college with a Bachelor’s degree and two years of relevant professional experience in strategic planning, program management, organizational development, higher education administration or a related field is required. A Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Public Administration, Business Administration, Organizational Leadership, Education or a related field is preferred. Demonstrated experience managing complex, cross-functional projects or strategic initiatives from planning through implementation and evaluation is also preferred. Candidate must have excellent project management, organizational, analytical, problem-solving and communication skills and proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and other technology used for project management, data analysis, reporting and presentations.   Candidacy review begins immediately and continues until appointment is made.   Please submit your cover letter, resume/CV and contact information for three professional references. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment.   In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the annual salary range for this position is: $78,000 to $95,000. This position may also be eligible for a comprehensive benefits package, including health and dental insurance, a retirement plan and benefits for work life balance. For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Kean University Benefits website . Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Adjunct-Faculty--Department-of-Psychology_R4568": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Department of Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nPart time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. College of Liberal Arts, Department of Psychology Adjunct Faculty Kean University  in Union, New Jersey has grown into a comprehensive, global institution of higher education serving a diverse enrollment of nearly 19,0000 students worldwide. Kean creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research and impactful public engagement. Kean, a proud R2 Research University, continues its legacy as a top producer of teachers in New Jersey and is a growing educational hub in the fields of business, health care and technology. Its six colleges – the College of Business and Public Management; the College of Education; the College of Liberal Arts; the Dorothy and George Hennings College of Science, Mathematics and Technology; Michael Graves College; and the College of Health Professions and Human Services - offer more than 50 undergraduate degrees over a full range of academic subjects. Kean also offers six doctoral degree programs and more than 70 options for graduate study leading to master’s degrees, professional diplomas or certifications. The University is also a higher education innovator within the State of New Jersey, partnering with Ocean County College, in Toms River, New Jersey and Brookdale Community College, in Lincroft, New Jersey, to provide access for students to earn a bachelor’s degree from Kean. The Kean Skylands campus, located in Jefferson Township, New Jersey, is designed to serve as an outdoor living laboratory for field-based scientific study and other classroom and field instruction. We are excited to invite Adjunct applications for upcoming semesters. Please note that Adjunct faculty positions at Kean University are filled on an as-needed basis. Qualified candidates may be contacted if, and when, there is an available opening or possible future opening. Field of Psychology  –   to teach courses in the field of psychology at both the undergraduate and graduate level at the Union Campus, Jersey City or Kean Ocean campus. Areas of study include General Psychology, Statistics, Tests and Measurements, Research Methods and other specialty areas such as Physiological Psychology, Industrial and Organizational (IO) Psychology and Forensic Psychology. Marriage & Family Therapy – to teach courses such as Family Systems, Theories and Techniques, Foundations of Family Therapy, Marital Therapy, Treatment Issues in Couples and Family Therapy, Group Practice in Family Therapy, Human Diversity in Marriage and Family Therapy or Clinical Practium. Current active License Marriage and Family Therapist (LMFT) licensure is required. Candidates who are Qualified Supervisors in New Jersey is preferred. All adjunct positions are non-tenure track. They require a master’s degree in a related field and teaching experience unless otherwise indicated; candidates with an ABD, Ed.D., Ph.D. or other acceptable disciplinary doctorate are encouraged to apply. Proficiency in a Learning Management System is required, consistent with University guidelines. Adjunct faculty teaching one three (3) or four (4) credit class shall provide at least one (1) hour of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. An additional thirty (30) minutes of availability shall be provided for each additional class taught during the semester/session. Availability may be in person or virtual and shall be scheduled by the adjunct faculty member, taking into account student needs. Adjunct faculty teaching fewer than three (3) credits shall provide at least thirty (30) minutes of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. Regardless of the number of credits an Adjunct faculty member is teaching, they may, at their discretion, provide additional office hours beyond the amounts required. Kean University Adjuncts are paid in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement: Effective September 2025, the rate of pay is: $2,100 per credit. Effective September 2026, the rate of pay is: $2,225 per credit. Beginning in their 13th semester taught, Adjuncts receive an additional $75 per credit. Adjuncts are enrolled in a state administered retirement plan, when eligible, and may be eligible to enroll in the Part-Time State Health Benefits Program for medical and prescription drug coverage. Please visit this link for more information: Health Coverage for Adjuncts . Please submit a cover letter (indicating availability for days, evenings or weekends and preferred campus location), resume and contact information for three professional references . Review of applications will begin immediately and be on-going. Official transcripts are required before appointment. Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Part-time-Positions-at-KEAN-_R848": {
      "title": "Part-time Positions at KEAN!",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nPart time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. Kean University Part-time Positions   Kean University is seeking applicants for hourly, part-time employment opportunities at our multiple campus locations.   Part-time employees perform a variety of responsibilities and assist with special projects. We offer a variety of positions across different areas and departments, providing opportunities for individuals with a range of skills, interests and subject matter expertise. Positions are primarily available at the Union campus, with additional opportunities at Kean   Ocean and Kean Jersey City. Positions are temporary and filled on a semester-to-semester basis, up to a maximum of 15 hours per week. Some positions may be filled for a shorter time period, depending on department needs and work assignments. The work schedule may vary each semester  with most positions working daytime hours between 8 am and 5 pm; some positions may  require evening  and/or weekend hours. In compliance with New Jersey’s Pay Transparency Law, the salary range for this position begins at $18.00. This is a part-time, temporary, hourly position and since this advertisement sources applications for positions across Kean's multiple campus locations, the maximum hourly rate may be determined by position, discipline and available budget. Part-time, hourly employees are eligible for sick leave, in accordance with New Jersey's Earned Sick Leave Law . For a full overview of our benefits offerings, please refer to our Ke an University Benefits website .     Qualifications: A Bachelor's degree is required. Additionally, some positions require training or experience in a related field. Candidates should possess excellent oral and written communication skills, attention to detail, organizational skills, interpersonal skills and have suitable scheduling flexibility. Please submit your resume and cover letter including your hours of availability. Official transcripts are required prior to the starting date of employment. Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
    },
    "https://kean.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Kean/job/Union-New-Jersey/Adjunct-Faculty--Office-of-Student-Placement---Clinical-Experiences_R2097": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Office of Student Placement & Clinical Experiences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\nPart time\n\nExternal Applicant Instructions Please upload your resume/CV for automatic population of information to your Kean application. Your contact information, work experience and education will be automatically filled in. Please review all fields – you will need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and any other supporting documents you may wish to submit. College of Education, Office of Student Placement & Clinical Experiences Adjunct Faculty Kean University  in Union, New Jersey has grown into a comprehensive, global institution of higher education serving a diverse enrollment of nearly 19,0000 students worldwide. Kean creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research and impactful public engagement.   Kean, a proud R2 Research University, continues its legacy as a top producer of teachers in New Jersey and is a growing educational hub in the fields of business, health care and technology. Its six colleges – the College of Business and Public Management; the College of Education; the College of Liberal Arts; the Dorothy and George Hennings College of Science, Mathematics and Technology; Michael Graves College; and the College of Health Professions and Human Services - offer more than 50 undergraduate degrees over a full range of academic subjects. Kean also offers six doctoral degree programs and more than 70 options for graduate study leading to master’s degrees, professional diplomas or certifications.   The University is also a higher education innovator within the State of New Jersey, partnering with Ocean County College, in Toms River, New Jersey and Brookdale Community College, in Lincroft, New Jersey, to provide access for students to earn a bachelor’s degree from Kean. The Kean Skylands campus, located in Jefferson Township, New Jersey, is designed to serve as an outdoor living laboratory for field-based scientific study and other   classroom   and field instruction.   In October 2025, Kean University and New Jersey City University (NJCU) signed a definitive agreement advancing a merger between the two state universities. The merger will position Kean as a statewide anchor institution and strengthens our ability to serve New Jersey’s diverse student population and uplift communities through education. The merger is currently progressing through the appropriate levels of approval, with a goal   to complete   this process by July 1, 2026.    We are excited to invite Adjunct applications for upcoming semesters. Please note that Adjunct faculty positions at Kean University are filled on an as-needed basis. Qualified candidates may be contacted if, and when, there is an available opening or possible future opening.    Clinical Supervisor – The role of a clinical supervisor (Adjunct Faculty) position assists with the support and development in student’s knowledge, skills and/or dispositions during one or more of the stages of a student’s clinical placements. This position includes supervising, observing, mentoring and providing both formative and summative feedback to Kean clinical students on their classroom preparation performance supported by research, theory, best practices and aligned to performance competencies. Additional duties include developing the skills of students related to lesson planning, lesson delivery and assessment aligned to New Jersey Professional Standards for Teachers (NJPST), Interstate New Teacher Assessment and Support Consortium standards (InTASC), Kean’s College of Education Lesson Plan and performance-based assessment instructions. This position will serve as the primary contact for P-12 cooperating teachers and their clinical students with regard to communication, problem solving and, when needed, conducting additional observations/site visits or completing additional evaluations. Ongoing monitoring of completion of all assessments by cooperating teachers and interns is required throughout the semester. Candidates must hold New Jersey teacher certification, hold a master’s degree or have extensive P-12 classroom and/or administration experience. Preference will be given to candidates that hold certification (under a standard certificate) in the subject matter area of supervision. Candidates should have strong technology skills with Microsoft products or the Google suite of programs and be able to travel to educational settings to conduct observations. Preferred qualifications include experience with NJPST and InTASC standards and familiarity with Council for the Accreditation of Education Preparation (CAEP) and/or the Associate for Advancing Quality in Educator Preparation (AAQEP). This position takes place in off-site P-12 districts, schools and other education settings with additional periodic required in-person meetings and events at the Union and Kean Ocean campus. All adjunct positions are non-tenure track. They require a master’s degree in a related field and teaching experience unless otherwise indicated; candidates with an ABD, Ed.D., Ph.D. or other acceptable disciplinary doctorate are encouraged to apply. Proficiency in a Learning Management System is required, consistent with University guidelines. Adjunct faculty teaching one three (3) or four (4) credit class shall provide at least one (1) hour of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. An additional thirty (30) minutes of availability shall be provided for each additional class taught during the semester/session. Availability may be in person or virtual and shall be scheduled by the adjunct faculty member, taking into account student needs. Adjunct faculty teaching fewer than three (3) credits shall provide at least thirty (30) minutes of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. Regardless of the number of credits an Adjunct faculty member is teaching, they may, at their discretion, provide additional office hours beyond the amounts required. Kean University Adjuncts are paid in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement: Effective September 2024, the rate of pay is: $1,975 per credit. Effective September 2025, the rate of pay is: $2,100 per credit. Effective September 2026, the rate of pay is: $2,225 per credit. Beginning in their 13th semester taught, Adjuncts receive an additional $75 per credit. All adjunct positions are non-tenure track. They require a master’s degree in a related field and teaching experience unless otherwise indicated; candidates with an ABD, Ed.D., Ph.D. or other acceptable disciplinary doctorate are encouraged to apply. Proficiency in a Learning Management System is required, consistent with University guidelines. Adjunct faculty teaching one three (3) or four (4) credit class shall provide at least one (1) hour of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. An additional thirty (30) minutes of availability shall be provided for each additional class taught during the semester/session. Availability may be in person or virtual and shall be scheduled by the adjunct faculty member, taking into account student needs. Adjunct faculty teaching fewer than three (3) credits shall provide at least thirty (30) minutes of availability outside of the classroom per week for the duration of each semester/session taught by the adjunct faculty member. Regardless of the number of credits an Adjunct faculty member is teaching, they may, at their discretion, provide additional office hours beyond the amounts required. Kean University Adjuncts are paid in accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement:   Effective September 2025, the rate of pay is: $2,100 per credit.   Effective September 2026, the rate of pay is: $2,225 per credit.   Beginning in their 13th semester taught, Adjuncts receive an additional $75 per credit.   Adjuncts are enrolled in a state administered retirement plan, when eligible, and may be eligible to enroll in the Part-Time State Health Benefits Program for medical and prescription drug coverage. Please visit this link for more information:   Health Coverage for Adjuncts .   Please submit a cover letter (indicating availability for days, evenings or weekends and preferred campus location), resume and contact information for three professional references.  Review of applications will begin immediately and be on-going. Official transcripts are required before appointment. Attention current Kean University employees (including part-time Student Assistants, Graduate Assistants, Academic Specialists and Adjuncts): Please apply via the internal career site to ensure consideration as an internal candidate. To apply internally, please log into your Workday account and select the Career icon on your homepage to view available positions. Additional Information Employment at Kean requires working at any of our New Jersey campus locations or affiliated work sites, which may include, but not be limited to: the main campus in Union; Kean Ocean in Toms River; Kean Skylands in Jefferson Township; Kean Jersey City; Kean at Brookdale in Middletown Township; Manahawkin; Princeton; and Trenton.  Location assignments will be based on operational and university needs. Faculty may also be assigned to teach online classes for Kean Global. Kean University complies with the New Jersey First Act  (Senate Bill No. 1730, P.L. 2011, Chapter 70). Any individual newly hired by Kean University will be required to abide by this law and establish a principal residence in New Jersey. New employees will have a full 365 days to establish such residence, from the effective date of hire. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position, please refer to Section III.A. of our  Reasonable Accommodations Policy & Procedures .   Kean University participates in E-Verify. For further information about the E-Verify program, please click here:  E-Verify . Mission Statement Kean University, New Jersey’s first Urban Research University, creates a world-class, innovative and inclusive society through equity and excellence in teaching, learning, global research, and impactful public engagement. EEO/AA Statement Kean University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Veterans/Disability Employer"
